# Cursor Rules for Figma Plugin Development

## Key Resources
- Figma Plugin API: https://www.figma.com/plugin-docs/intro/
  - Use `figma` global object, JavaScript for logic, HTML/CSS for UI.
  - Handle async operations (e.g., `figma.loadFontAsync`).
- Plugin Review Guidelines: https://help.figma.com/hc/en-us/articles/360047285394
  - No crashes, accurate metadata, support contact in UI.
  - Avoid non-API external packages.
- Community Guidelines: https://help.figma.com/hc/en-us/articles/360039958634
  - No trademark misuse or offensive content.
- Standards of Conduct: https://www.figma.com/standards-of-conduct/
  - Secure data handling (e.g., OAuth2.0), legal compliance.
- Security: https://forum.figma.com/t/security-considerations-when-deploying-plugin/39182
  - Secure OAuth2.0, safe fileKey handling.
- MCP Server: https://github.com/figma/mcp-server
  - Run `npx fig2ai <figma-design-url>` for `.designrules`.

## Coding Standards
- Language: JavaScript (logic), HTML/CSS (UI).
- API: Use `figma` object for interactions.
- UI: Render via `figma.showUI`, handle `figma.ui.onmessage`.
- Security: Secure OAuth2.0, data handling.
- Testing: Error handling, test for crashes.
- Dependencies: No non-API external packages.
- Metadata: Accurate name, description, support contact.

## Cursor Instructions
- Generate code compliant with above resources.
- Validate against Plugin Review Guidelines.
- Use `.designrules` from MCP server for design context.
- Audit security (OAuth2.0, fileKey).
- Align UI/metadata with Brand/Community Guidelines.